A participant P 2 P is an essential participant if there exists a set X  P such that
X [ fP g 2 Qual but X 62 Qual . If a participant P is not essential then we can construct
a visual cryptography scheme giving him a share completely \white" or even nothing as
his share. In fact, a non-essential participant does not need to participate \actively" in the
reconstruction of the image, since the information he has is not needed by any set in P
in order to recover the shared image. In any VCS having non-essential participants, these
participants do not require any information in their shares. Therefore, unless otherwise
speci ed, we assume throughout this paper that all participants are essential.
     In the case where Qual is monotone increasing, Forb is monotone decreasing, and
  Qual [ Forb = 2 , the access structure is said to be strong, and 0 is termed a basis. (This
                       P
situation is the usual setting for traditional secret sharing.) In a strong access structure,
